# Model selection (default)

Without the user **manually selecting** a model in the UI or **explicitly naming** a model in the prompt, use **only Cursor models**. Do not pick Claude, GPT, Gemini, or any other non-Cursor model on your own.

## Default tiers

| Task class | Model | Slug (subagents / Task) |
|------------|--------|-------------------------|
| Simple / small | Composer 2.5 | `composer-2.5-fast` |
| High-value (planning, orchestration, multi-phase design) | Cursor Grok 4.6 | `cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast` |

**Simple / small:** typo fixes, single-file edits, short answers, mechanical refactors, status checks, one-shot lookups.

**High-value:** Plan mode / nawab-plans, architecture, multi-repo orchestration, long-horizon agent design, trade-off-heavy decisions, coordinating multiple subagents.

When spawning subagents, pass the matching slug above. Default to Composer 2.5 if unsure; escalate to Grok 4.6 only when the work is clearly high-value.

## Overrides

Allowed only when the user:

1. Selects a different model in the Cursor UI for this chat, or
2. Explicitly asks in the prompt (e.g. "use Claude", "use GPT", a specific slug)

Do not infer permission from past chats, defaults elsewhere, or "best model for X" habit. If they ask which model to use, recommend from the table - do not switch until they confirm.
